oward candidates favored by the bug and sustain meaningful improvement in the visible metrics.", "validation_plan_suggested_by_judge": "Run the next optimization iteration with design_cost removed; the validator should observe no extreme out-of-range scores, and continued improvement in parameter_mean (move toward 0.5) and parameter_spread (increase or maintain exploration). If acceptable, later reintroduce design_cost after fixing/validating its outputs.", "self_reported_confidence_uncalibrated": 0.8, "target_assessment": null}, "notes": [], "judge_raw_output": "The analyzer shows clear, objective evidence that the design_cost scorer is producing out-of-range/invalid values (mean = -6.5903e10 \u00b1 1.8916e10, best = -7.2005e10, worst = 1.0) which contradicts the documented [0,1] range and will corrupt selection. The two parameter-based objectives are behaving sensibly and improving. The cheapest, lowest-risk corrective action is to temporarily remove the broken design_cost objective so the optimizer continues making meaningful progress on the reliable objectives while the scorer is fixed.\n\n<decision>\n{\n  \"failure_location\": \"implementation\",\n  \"root_cause_hypothesis\": \"The design_cost scorer is producing out-of-range/overflowed values (huge negative numbers and mixed 1.0s) due to a scorer normalization/overflow or evaluation-failure mode; uncertain until the scorer is inspected.\",\n  \"intervention_target\": \"objective\",\n  \"rationale\": \"design_cost reported mean = -6.5903e10 \u00b1 1.8916e10, best = -7.2005e10, worst = 1.0 \u2014 these values contradict the documented [0,1] range and will dominate/mislead selection. parameter_mean and parameter_spread show sensible improvement (parameter_mean mean = 0.5238 \u00b1 0.0766; parameter_spread mean = 0.3718 \u00b1 0.0256). Temporarily removing the broken objective is low-risk and conforms to the analyzer recommendation.\",\n  \"proposed_change\": {\n    \"ops\": [\n      {\n        \"op\": \"drop\",\n        \"name\": \"design_cost\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"expected_benefit\": \"Removes corrupted/heterogeneous design_cost scores from selection, allowing optimization to proceed guided by the two reliable objectives (parameter_mean and parameter_spread). This should prevent spurious convergence toward candidates favored by the bug and sustain meaningful improvement in the visible metrics.\",\n  \"validation_plan\": \"Run the next optimization iteration with design_cost removed; the validator should observe no extreme out-of-range scores, and continued improvement in parameter_mean (move toward 0.5) and parameter_spread (increase or maintain exploration). If acceptable, later reintroduce design_cost after fixing/validating its outputs.\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.80\n}\n</decision>", "change_id": "2e0b40b06648456a", "candidate_state": {"version": 0, "planner_guidance": null, "objective_ops": [{"op": "drop", "name": "design_cost"}], "implementation_patches": {}, "workflow_params": {}}, "validation": {"seeds": [3000, 3001], "use_planner": false, "candidate_objectives": ["parameter_mean", "parameter_spread"], "baseline_objectives": ["design_cost", "parameter_mean", "parameter_spread"], "baseline": [0.0007063976155606168, 0.00015452620619180055], "candidate": [1.928982568129226e-06, 2.0365840165383057e-06], "baseline_mean": 0.0004304619108762087, "candidate_mean": 1.9827832923337656e-06, "delta": -0.00042847912758387494, "min_improvement": 0.02, "candidate_constraint_violation": false, "details": {"baseline": [{"split": "validation", "top_k": 5, "top_k_by_true_quality": 0.004781025250478309, "population_mean": 0.0011163404691623179, "best": 0.007576467191373114, "n_invalid": 0}, {"split": "validation", "top_k": 5, "top_k_by_true_quality": 0.0018141365715820825, "population_mean": 0.00029835432955198186, "best": 0.007745402155581098, "n_invalid": 0}], "candidate": [{"split": "validation", "top_k": 5, "top_k_by_true_quality": 7.460394037077356e-06, "population_mean": 3.60